{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Convex.SelfDualCone\n\n/-!\n# Projective aliases for self-dual cones\n\nThis module is the projective-facing API layer over the Mathlib-rooted cone\nprimitives in `InfoGeometry.Convex.SelfDualCone`.  The historical names remain\nas abbreviations, so downstream projective modules keep their low-level API\nwhile the proof root is the single Convex/Mathlib chain rather than a duplicate\nstructure.\n-/\n\nnoncomputable section\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Projective\n\nopen scoped Projectivization\n\nvariable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n\n/-- Projective-facing alias for the Mathlib-rooted self-dual cone structure. -/\nabbrev SelfDualCone (E : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] : Type _ :=\n  InfoGeometry.Convex.SelfDualCone E\n\n/-- The state space formed by rays in the interior of a proper cone. -/\nabbrev ConeInteriorStateSpace (C : ProperCone ℝ E) : Type _ :=\n  InfoGeometry.Convex.ConeInteriorRay (E := E) C\n\n/-- The space of rays on the boundary or interior of a proper cone. -/\nabbrev ConeBoundaryRaySpace (C : ProperCone ℝ E) : Type _ :=\n  InfoGeometry.Convex.ConeRay (E := E) C\n\n/-- Read back the Mathlib `ProperCone.innerDual` equality from a projective-facing cone. -/\n@[simp] theorem SelfDualCone.innerDual_eq [CompleteSpace E] (C : SelfDualCone E) :\n    ProperCone.innerDual (C.cone : Set E) = C.cone :=\n  InfoGeometry.Convex.SelfDualCone.innerDual_eq C\n\n/-- Read back a nonzero interior representative from the projective state-space alias. -/\ntheorem ConeInteriorStateSpace.exists_rep {C : ProperCone ℝ E}\n    (ℓ : ConeInteriorStateSpace (E := E) C) :\n    ∃ v : E, ∃ hv : v ≠ 0, v ∈ interior (C : Set E) ∧\n      Projectivization.mk ℝ v hv = ℓ.1 :=\n  ℓ.2\n\n/-- Read back a nonzero representative from the projective boundary-ray alias. -/\ntheorem ConeBoundaryRaySpace.exists_rep {C : ProperCone ℝ E}\n    (ℓ : ConeBoundaryRaySpace (E := E) C) :\n    ∃ v : E, ∃ hv : v ≠ 0, v ∈ (C : Set E) ∧ Projectivization.mk ℝ v hv = ℓ.1 :=\n  ℓ.2\n\nend InfoGeometry.Projective\n","mtime":1778318585833}